## 1. Executive Summary & Brutal MVP Technical Due Diligence

The provided `MediScan` codebase represents an early-stage prototype (Tier-0 Proof of Concept) built across three disconnected, conflicting paradigms: an Anvil Uplink script (`anvil_server.py`, `client_code/*`), a single-threaded Streamlit script (`app.py`), a development-mode Flask wrapper (`flask_app.py`), and static HTML/Tailwind mockups (`index.html`, `mediscan_*`).

From the perspective of a Chief Technology Officer preparing for institutional Series A/B funding, enterprise hospital procurement, and FDA/CE/CDSCO regulatory scrutiny, **100% of the existing runtime architecture must be deprecated and rewritten.** Deploying the current codebase in a live clinical environment poses immediate patient safety hazards, severe legal liabilities, and catastrophic security vulnerabilities.

