## 7. Deployment Architecture (Global Multi-Region & Enterprise Hybrid)

Healthcare regulations strictly forbid cross-border transfer of identifiable patient health data in many jurisdictions (e.g., India's DPDP Act, EU GDPR + national health laws, Saudi PDPL, US HIPAA). Furthermore, Tier-1 hospital chains often refuse to send raw PACS DICOM streams or live ICU waveforms over the public internet.

MediScan solves this via a **Two-Tier Control/Data Plane Architecture**:

1. **Regional Sovereign Cloud Pods (SaaS Multi-Tenant & Single-Tenant Dedicated):** Independent, self-contained Kubernetes (EKS/GKE) data planes deployed in `us-east-1` / `us-west-2` (USA), `eu-central-1` (Frankfurt), `ap-south-1` (Mumbai), and `me-central-1` (UAE). Zero PHI ever crosses regional boundaries.
2. **Hospital On-Premises Edge Appliance ("MediScan Edge Box"):** For enterprise hospital networks, MediScan deploys an **AWS Outposts / Google Distributed Cloud Virtual / K3s GPU Appliance** (2x NVIDIA L40S GPUs) inside the hospital's local DMZ. It processes PACS DICOM studies, HL7v2 MLLP feeds, and de-identification locally, syncing only encrypted, consented clinical metadata or federated model gradients to the regional cloud.

