## 8. Model Lifecycle & MLOps Architecture

In regulated healthcare (FDA **Predetermined Change Control Plan - PCCP** and **IEC 62304**), you cannot simply run `model.fit()` on startup as `server_code/model.py` does. Every model weight, training dataset slice, hyperparameter, and evaluation metric must be cryptographically versioned, clinically validated across demographic subgroups, and deployed via canary/shadow gates.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Hospital EHR, PACS & Wearable Streams"] --> B["Automated De-Identification Pipeline<br/>(Microsoft Presidio + DICOM Pixel Scrubbing)"]
    B --> C["Apache Iceberg Lakehouse + Feast Feature Store<br/>(DVC / LakeFS Data Version Control)"]
    C --> D["Distributed Model Training<br/>(PyTorch Lightning / Ray Train / Federated Learning via Flower)"]
    D --> E["MLflow Model Registry<br/>(Signed Safetensors + SBOM + Training Lineage)"]
    
    subgraph "Clinical & Regulatory Validation Gate (CI/CD)"
        E --> F{"Automated Evaluation Harness"}
        F -->|Check 1| G["Clinical Accuracy & Calibration<br/>(AUROC, AUPRC, Brier Score, ECE < 0.02)"]
        F -->|Check 2| H["Demographic Fairness Audit<br/>(Equalized Odds across Age, Sex, Race, Socioeconomic)"]
        F -->|Check 3| I["Adversarial & LLM Red-Teaming<br/>(Med-HALT Hallucination, Prompt Injection, Negation)"]
    end

    G & H & I --> J{"Clinical Safety Board<br/>Cryptographic Sign-Off?"}
    J -->|Rejected| D
    J -->|Approved| K["Shadow Deployment (Dark Launch)<br/>Runs silently on 100% live traffic vs. Production Model"]
    K --> L["Canary Rollout (5% -> 25% -> 100%)<br/>via Argo Rollouts & KServe / Triton"]
    L --> M["Continuous Drift & RLHF Monitoring<br/>(EvidentlyAI + Arize Phoenix + Clinician Overrides)"]
    M -->|PSI > 0.2 or Override Spike| C

```

1. **Zero-Retraining on Unverified Outputs:** Clinician edits to SOAP notes and overrides on CDS drug alerts are captured as structured **Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF / DPO)** preference pairs, reviewed by an internal clinical informatics panel before entering the golden training corpus.
2. **Federated Learning (NVIDIA FLARE / Flower):** Allows MediScan to train and fine-tune diagnostic models across 50+ partner hospitals without raw patient data ever leaving the hospital's on-premises servers. Only differentially private ($\epsilon$-DP) weight gradients are aggregated centrally.

