## 11. Data Governance, Privacy & Zero-Trust Security Strategy

* **Global Privacy Regulatory Matrix:**
* **United States:** Full **HIPAA** Security & Privacy Rules, **HITECH**, **21st Century Cures Act** (Information Blocking compliance), and **SOC 2 Type II + HITRUST r2** certification.
* **European Union:** **GDPR** (Articles 9 & 22—Right to explanation for automated decisions, Right to erasure/rectification) and the **European Health Data Space (EHDS)**.
* **India:** **Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023**, **ABDM Health Data Management Policy**, and **CERT-In** directives.


* **Cryptographic Envelope Encryption & Pseudonymization:**
* Every tenant (hospital system) is assigned a dedicated **Customer Managed Key (CMK)** in **AWS KMS / HashiCorp Vault (FIPS 140-3 Level 3 HSM)**.
* Every patient record has a unique **Data Encryption Key (DEK)**. If a patient exercises their GDPR/DPDP "Right to be Forgotten" (where legally permissible outside mandatory medical record retention windows), MediScan executes **Crypto-Shredding**—destroying the patient's specific DEK, rendering all historical backups of their PII permanently unreadable without mutating immutable WORM audit archives.


* **Automated PHI De-Identification Pipeline:**
* Before any clinical data enters the analytics lakehouse (`Apache Iceberg`) or ML training cluster, it passes through a **HIPAA Safe Harbor & Expert Determination De-Identification Pipeline**:
* **Text/Transcripts:** **Microsoft Presidio** + fine-tuned **Clinical-DeID-RoBERTa** strips all 18 HIPAA identifiers (names, dates shifted by a patient-consistent random offset $\Delta t \in [-30, +30]\text{ days}$, phone numbers, MRNs, geographic subdivisions smaller than a state).
* **DICOM Medical Images:** Strips all PII DICOM header tags (`(0010,0010) PatientName`, `(0010,0020) PatientID`) and runs an automated **Optical Character Recognition (OCR) Pixel Masking pass** to black out burned-in patient names/dates on ultrasound and portable X-ray pixels.
* **Voice Audio:** Applies **Voice Anonymization (Pitch/Formant Shifting via McAdams coefficient transformation)** so raw audio cannot be biometrically matched back to the patient's voiceprint while preserving clinical speech content.




* **Zero-Trust Runtime Security:**
* **Identity:** Phishing-resistant **FIDO2 / WebAuthn Passkeys** + Smartcard badge tap (Imprivata integration) for clinicians. Short-lived JWTs (5-minute TTL) with continuous session risk scoring.
* **Network:** **Istio Service Mesh** with strict `STRICT` mTLS between all pods, **Cilium eBPF** kernel-level network policies, and **Runtime Security (Falco / Tetragon)** alerting on any unexpected shell execution or file-system read inside a container.
* **"Break-the-Glass" Emergency Access:** If an ER physician needs to access the chart of an unconscious patient not assigned to their department, the system permits instant override access but immediately fires a high-priority alert to the Hospital Privacy Officer and logs the justification in the hash-chained `immutable_audit_ledger`.



